From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:23:26 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] cpu-governor

General gains a CPU row (Performance, Balanced), stored as `mode = balanced`
in Config/cpu.txt. Performance is the default and writes performance, as
BaseOS already runs. Balanced writes schedutil to every cpufreq policy at
start and when the row changes, after checking each policy offers it.
Every write logs `slot: cpu:` with what each policy reads back.

Idea from pvaibhav/slot ad7ce10 and 320ac44 (launch_frontend.sh writes
schedutil), GPL-3.0, Copyright Prashant Vaibhav; here it is a user option.

(cherry picked from commit c2c77a9cfa70ceb9be6a03f34259d3441cf46bf7)
